  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">United Nations Development Programme, Iran - Iran (Islamic Republic) (01-Apr-2015-31-Mar-2018)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Iran (Islamic Republic), HIV, United Nations Development Programme (UNDP Iran)This program has the following goals: Decreased AIDS mortality rate in identified HIV positive cases by 20%..  Decreased rate of HIV prevalence among newborns of HIV infected mothers who delivered in the past 12 months by 90%.  Maintaining the HIV prevalence rate among men and women with the most high-risk sexual behaviors at less than 5%.  Maintaining the HIV prevalence rate at less than 13% among IDUs. The objectives of this program are: Objective 1: By the end of 2019, at least 95% of the IDUs should use sterilized and non-shared devices for injection in their last injection.  Objective 2: By the end of 2019, the percentage of VW who have used condom in their latest last sexual contact should reach 60%.  Objective 3: By the end of 2019, 90% of the estimated pregnant women infected with HIV should be covered by standard treatments in line with prevention of mother-to-child transmission.  Objective 4: By the end of 2019, more than 90% of the advanced HIV/AIDS infection cases who have started their treatment a year ago, will adhere to treatment</narrative>
  </description>
